# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT ignored. The build stage derives the version
# string from `git describe`, and excluding .git here would silently turn every
# published image's version into "dev".
#
# For the same reason, nothing TRACKED may be ignored either. Go stamps
# vcs.modified by comparing the build tree against .git, so stripping a tracked
# file makes every image report "[dirty]" while the release tarball built from
# the same commit does not -- and buildinfo.go prints that suffix. `.github/`,
# `*.md` and `.gitignore` used to be here and cost 11 tracked files; the context
# they save is a few kilobytes of text.

vendor/
tags
.bin/
run.sh

# Build output. `mtg` is the pre-rename binary name; the current one is
# mtg-proxy, and the release workflow also produces mtg-proxy-<version>-*
# archives and a dist/ directory. Copying a host-built binary into the build
# context is how a stale or foreign artifact ends up in an image.
mtg
mtg-proxy
mtg-proxy-*
dist/
*.exe
*.test
coverage.txt
